# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: WarriorPath | Scene: WarriorQueen7Calshure

translate es strings:

    old "Sarah sat atop one of the battlements of the city of Calshure."
    new "Sarah se sentó sobre uno de los almenados de la ciudad de Calshure."

    old "With exception of the keep, most of the buildings in Calshure were build quite low, allowing her to look over the entire city."
    new "Con la excepción de la fortaleza, la mayoría de los edificios en Calshure eran bastante bajos, lo que le permitía ver toda la ciudad."

    old "She watched her army marching through the streets of the city, greeted as liberators."
    new "Ella observó a su ejército marchar por las calles de la ciudad, recibido como libertadores."

    old "The Tribesmen had fled the city by early hour, keeping true to their word."
    new "Los tribus huyeron de la ciudad antes del amanecer, cumpliendo su palabra."

    old "The City Guard had opened the gates to the city, allowing her army to enter without so much as drawing steel."
    new "La Guardia Ciudadana había abierto las puertas de la ciudad, permitiendo que su ejército entrara sin siquiera sacar el acero."

    old "Most of the Tribesmen had died in the battle."
    new "La mayoría de los tribales murieron en la batalla."

    old "A rare few were caught alive, mostly becaused they had been too wounded to fight to their deaths."
    new "Pocos lograron sobrevivir, mayormente porque habían sido demasiado heridos para luchar hasta morir."

    old "For them, being captured was worse than death."
    new "Para ellos, ser capturados era peor que la muerte."

    old "Denied their glory."
    new "Negada su gloria."

    old "Sarah watched as people threw themselves as the soldiers of her army."
    new "Sarah observó cómo la gente se arrojaba contra los soldados de su ejército."

    old "Crying, desperate gratitude."
    new "Llorando, una desesperada gratitud."

    old "It was hard for her to imagine what these people must have endured."
    new "Le resultaba difícil imaginarse qué debían haber sufrido esas personas."

    old "To have lived under the control of the Tribesmen for years on end. Enduring their rule."
    new "Vivir bajo el control de los Tribales durante años enteros. Soportar su dominio."

    old "From the corner of her eyes, Sarah saw a man walk up towards her."
    new "Desde la esquina de su vista, Sarah vio a un hombre acercarse hacia ella."

    old "His bronzed skin and un-Rosannan garb set him apart from most."
    new "Su piel bronceada y su vestimenta no rosannana lo distinguían de la mayoría."

    old "Cassius."
    new "Cassius."

    old "I wondered where you might be."
    new "Me preguntaba dónde podrías estar."

    old "The people are eager to meet you. It's all they talk about."
    new "La gente está ansiosa por conocerte. Es de lo que siempre hablan."

    old "Sarah sighed. She was tired."
    new "Sarah suspiró. Estaba cansada."

    old "I'll be down in a moment. I'm just...taking a breather."
    new "Bajaré en un momento. Solo... necesito recuperar el aliento."

    old "No rush. They'll wait up all day if they have to, just to catch a glimpse."
    new "No hay prisa. Esperarán todo el día si es necesario, solo para verlos."

    old "Their great liberator."
    new "Su gran libertador."

    old "Is that what they're saying?"
    new "¿Es eso lo que dicen?"

    old "Cassius nodded again."
    new "Cassius asintió de nuevo."

    old "Yeah."
    new "Sí."

    old "I've been out among the citizens for a bit. Heard some stories of what it was like."
    new "He estado entre los ciudadanos un rato. He oído algunas historias sobre cómo era eso."

    old "If even half of it was true, then I can't blame them for being happy to be rid of the Tribesmen."
    new "Si incluso la mitad de eso era cierto, no puedo culparlos por estar contentos de deshacerse de los hombres de las tribus."

    old "Cassius spat."
    new "Cassius escupió."

    old "Savage creatures."
    new "Criaturas salvajes."

    old "Wish you'd given me a chance to meet them in battle though."
    new "¡Deseaba que me hubieras dado la oportunidad de conocerlos en combate!"

    old "What? Not a fan of the diplomatic option?"
    new "¿Qué? ¿No te gusta la opción diplomática?"

    old "I am a warrior first."
    new "Soy un guerrero primero."

    old "If all the rulers of the world were like you, I'd never find work again."
    new "Si todos los gobernantes del mundo fueran como tú, nunca volvería a encontrar trabajo."

    old "Yes, a tragedy."
    new "Sí, una tragedia."

    old "Then you'd have to get a real vocation."
    new "Entonces tendrías que buscar una verdadera vocación."

    old "Ah, yes. A farmer perhaps. Can you imagine me with a pitchfork?"
    new "Ah, sí. Un campesino, quizás. ¿Puedes imaginarme con una horca?"

    old "You would make a terrible farmer."
    new "Haces un pésimo agricultor."

    old "Still, they make for good practice."
    new "Aun así, sirven de buen ejercicio."

    old "Sarah looked at him and saw a few scratches on his body."
    new "Sarah lo miró y vio algunas rasguños en su cuerpo."

    old "Don't tell me they gave you any trouble."
    new "No me digas que te han jodido."

    old "Nothing so serious, but they're interesting fighters. Unique styles."
    new "Nada tan grave, pero son luchadores interesantes. Estilos únicos."

    old "Well, glad you got your fun out of it."
    new "Bueno, me alegra que hayas sacado tu diversión."

    old "And the dead?"
    new "¿Y los muertos?"

    old "The dead have won glory. Might we all be so lucky one day."
    new "La muerte ha ganado gloria. ¿Podríamos todos tener tanta suerte algún día?"

    old "Sarah couldn't tell if he was joking or serious. Perhaps both."
    new "Sarah no podía decir si estaba bromeando o siendo serio. Quizás ambas cosas."

    old "Anyway, I just thought I'd let you know that they're ready for you in the main square."
    new "De todos modos, solo quería avisarte que ya están listos para ti en la plaza principal."

    old "Thanks. I'll be down in just a bit."
    new "Gracias. Estaré abajo en un momento."

    old "She watched Cassius leave again."
    new "La observó irse de nuevo."

    old "Below she could hearing the growing murmurs of the crowd, gathering."
    new "Abajo, podía oír los murmullos crecientes de la multitud que se reunía."

    old "She felt more hestitant to meet her own people than to meet her enemies on the battlefield."
    new "Se sentía más indecisa para encontrarse con su propio pueblo que para enfrentarse a sus enemigos en el campo de batalla."

    old "But this too was a part of ruling."
    new "Pero esto también era parte de gobernar."

    old "Sarah pushed herself to her feet and began to make her way down the steps of the walls."
    new "Sarah se impulsó de pie y comenzó a descender por los escalones de las murallas."

    old "Below, she could see the growing crowd, shouting and screaming as they began to spot her."
    new "Abajo, podía ver la multitud creciente, gritando y chillando mientras comenzaban a localizarla."

    old "She slightly waved."
    new "Hizo un leve gesto con la mano."

    old "Even that smallest of gesture was enough to solicit a roar from the crowd."
    new "Incluso ese gesto más pequeño fue suficiente para provocar un rugido en la multitud."

    old "As she descended from the last flight of stairs, she stepped out onto the improvised podium that had been build."
    new "A medida que descendía de la última escalera, salió al podio improvisado que había montado."

    old "Slowly she walked out onto the stage."
    new "Lentamente, salió al escenario."

    old "With each step, the crowd grew louder and louder."
    new "Con cada paso, la multitud se hacía más ruidosa."

    old "She saw the square, filled with people, pressing up against one another, screaming out her name."
    new "Vio la plaza llena de gente, apretándose los unos contra los otros, gritando su nombre."

    old "As she looked over the crowd of people, she saw not just the whole of them, but the individuals."
    new "Mientras observaba la multitud, no solo veía el conjunto de las personas, sino a cada individuo."

    old "The desperate, pleading eyes from and old man."
    new "Los ojos desesperados y suplicantes de un anciano."

    old "The cheering, rapturous screams from a younger one."
    new "Los gritos jodidos y extáticos de uno más joven."

    old "An older woman, crying, clutching what seemed to be her daughter."
    new "Una mujer mayor, llorando, aferrada a lo que parecía ser su hija."

    old "So many different people, all brought together."
    new "Tantas personas diferentes, todas reunidas."

    old "Around her."
    new "A su alrededor."

    old "Sarah trembled at the realization that all this worship on their faces was for her."
    new "Sarah tembló al darse cuenta de que toda esa adoración en sus rostros era para ella."

    old "Was she really worthy of this?"
    new "¿Era realmente digna de esto?"

    old "Could any person be?"
    new "¿Podría ser cualquier persona?"

    old "Memories of her Father came to her. He had seemed worthy of it, in her estimation."
    new "Memorias de su padre llegaron a ella. Él había parecido digno de ello, en su juicio."

    old "But to compare herself to her Father still seemed to her mind as blasphemous."
    new "Pero compararse a su Padre seguía pareciéndole blasfemo."

    old "Her people..."
    new "Su gente..."

    old "Sarah raised one fist in the air, motioning the crowd to silence."
    new "Sarah levantó un puño en el aire, señalando a la multitud para que callara."

    old "Slowly, their cheers drifted away to whispers, and finally to silence."
    new "Lentamente, sus algarabías se desvanecieron en susurros y finalmente en silencio."

    old "The whole of the city seemed suddenly still."
    new "El conjunto de la ciudad pareció repentinamente inmóvil."

    old "People of Calshure!"
    new "¡Pueblo de Calshure!"

    old "People of Rosanna!"
    new "¡Pueblo de Rosanna!"

    old "The tyranny of the Tribes is over!"
    new "¡La tiranía de las Tribus ha terminado!"

    old "Her declaration was met with loud cheers from the gathered citizens."
    new "Su declaración fue acogida con estruendosas ovaciones por los ciudadanos reunidos."

    old "Before today, most of you had never seen me."
    new "Antes de hoy, la mayoría de ustedes nunca me habían visto."

    old "But you have heard my name."
    new "Pero has oído mi nombre."

    old "You have heard the name of my family."
    new "Has oído el nombre de mi familia."

    old "Rose."
    new "Rose."

    old "Sarah studied their faces, seeing their recognition."
    new "Sarah estudió sus rostros, viendo su reconocimiento."

    old "I come before you, not to demand loyalty like kings of old, but to ask for your aid."
    new "Vengo ante ti no para exigir lealtad como los reyes de antaño, sino para pedirte tu ayuda."

    old "We have won a great victory today, but this war is not yet over."
    new "Hemos obtenido una gran victoria hoy, pero esta guerra aún no ha terminado."

    old "Not while a foreign warlord sits upon the Throne of my family."
    new "No mientras un caudillo extranjero ocupe el Trono de mi familia."

    old "Angry shouts could be heard across the square."
    new "Se podían escuchar gritos furiosos en toda la plaza."

    old "Oaths of loyalty are easily sworn, and we speak them sometimes without thinking."
    new "Los juramentos de lealtad se prestan con facilidad, y a veces los pronunciamos sin pensarlo."

    old "But it is in times of great crisis, like the one we find ourselves in, that we are forced to confront the simple truths."
    new "Pero es en tiempos de gran crisis, como la que nos encontramos, cuando estamos obligados a confrontar las simples verdades."

    old "Who has sworn oaths whose words weigh less than air."
    new "¿Quién ha jurado votos cuyas palabras pesan menos que el aire?"

    old "And who here, by uttering their oaths, have wedded themselves to Nation and People, as surely as vows of marriage wed two souls to one another?"
    new "¿Y quiénes, aquí presentes, al pronunciar sus juramentos, se han casado con la Nación y el Pueblo, tan seguro como los votos matrimoniales unen dos almas en una sola?"

    old "Loud, approving cries, rose up from the crowd."
    new "¡Gritos de alabanza resonaron entre la multitud!"

    old "Then I say to all of you today, with this war not yet won; I shall demand none of you to fight by threat of conscription."
    new "Entonces digo a todos hoy, con esta guerra aún no ganada; no exigiré de ninguno que pelee bajo amenaza de reclutamiento."

    old "I ask only..."
    new "Solo pido..."

    old "Whom here pledges their lives willingly?"
    new "¿Quién aquí promete su vida voluntariamente?"

    old "A thunderous chorus rose up."
    new "Un coro ensordecedor se alzó."

    old "Sarah watched as men leapt, throwing up their arms, eager to join her army."
    new "Sarah observó cómo los hombres saltaban, alzando sus brazos, ansiosos por unirse a su ejército."

    old "She smiled, seeing how her army would swell from the influx of these new and eager recruits."
    new "Sonrió al ver cómo su ejército se reforzaría con la llegada de estos nuevos y ansiosos reclutas."

    old "Not trained in war, but any capeable hand could learn to swing a sword."
    new "No entrenados en la guerra, pero cualquier mano capaz podría aprender a manejar una espada."

    old "And any eager man could be trained to kill."
    new "Y cualquier hombre ansioso podía ser entrenado para matar."

    old "She saw their faces painted with mad zeal, eager for war."
    new "Vio sus rostros pintados con un fanatismo loco, ansiosos por la guerra."

    old "And she would give them their desires."
    new "Y les daría sus deseos."

    old "A few hours had passed and night had fallen over the city of Calshure."
    new "Pasadas unas horas, la noche había caído sobre la ciudad de Calshure."

    old "Sarah was sitting behind her desk, working at preparing the orders to resume the march."
    new "Sarah se sentaba detrás de su escritorio, trabajando en preparar las órdenes para reanudar la marcha."

    old "Outside, she could hear the loud celebrations."
    new "Fuera, podía oír las celebraciones ruidosas."

    old "Her soldiers were eager for some relaxation, and the citizens were overflowing with gratitude from being liberated from the Tribesmen."
    new "Sus soldados ansiaban un poco de descanso y los ciudadanos desbordaban gratitud por haber sido liberados de los Tribusmen."

    old "From what few reports she had read, their occupation had been brutal."
    new "Según los pocos informes que había leído, su ocupación había sido brutal."

    old "The Tribesmen had never truly intended to rule over the land or the people. Not as genuine rulers."
    new "Los tribus nunca habían pretendido gobernar la tierra o al pueblo. No como gobernantes auténticos."

    old "They simply sat in their halls, extracting wealth and women, and putting down any resistance with brute force."
    new "Simplemente se sentaban en sus salones, extrayendo riqueza y mujeres, y aplastando cualquier resistencia con fuerza bruta."

    old "Meanwhile, the yields of the nearby farms had collapsed and the local economy had likewise dwindled."
    new "Mientras tanto, las cosechas de las granjas cercanas habían colapsado y la economía local también se había encogido."

    old "Planting crops and raising livestock meant believing in a stable future."
    new "Plantar cultivos y criar ganado significaba creer en un futuro estable."

    old "The Tribesmen simply raided as they pleased."
    new "Los tribales simplemente saqueaban como les daba la gana."

    old "Poverty. Starvation. Exploitation."
    new "Pobreza. Hambre. Explotación."

    old "These were all the Tribesmen had brought to her people."
    new "Estos eran todos los que las tribus habían traído a su pueblo."

    old "And they had forever remained foreign to the people of Rosanna."
    new "Y permanecieron para siempre ajenos al pueblo de Rosanna."

    old "They kept locked to their own keeps, having little interest in the people outside of what they could extract from them."
    new "Mantuvieron sus fortalezas bajo llave, mostrando poco interés en las personas fuera de lo que podían extraer de ellas."

    old "And thus, there seemed few people if any in the city of Calshure that were sad to see the Tribesmen gone."
    new "Y así, parecían pocos, si no nadie, en la ciudad de Calshure que estuviera triste por ver a los tribales marcharse."

    old "Sarah continued her work."
    new "Sarah continuó su labor."

    old "There was so much to do."
    new "Había tanto por hacer."

    old "She'd leave the celebrations to other people."
    new "Dejaría las celebraciones a otras personas."

    old "She had to keep her momentum. Continue to march on the Capital as soon as possible."
    new "Tenía que mantener su impulso. Marchar sobre la Capital lo antes posible."

    old "The new recruits from Calshure would be a welcome addition to her army."
    new "Los nuevos reclutas de Calshure serían una bienvenida adición a su ejército."

    old "Sarah went over a report from the chief medic."
    new "Sarah revisó un informe del médico jefe."

    old "They were already running dangerously low on medical supplies, just to deal with those currently wounded."
    new "Ya estaban agotando peligrosamente sus suministros médicos, solo para atender a los heridos que había."

    old "The wounded soldiers lined up outside the triage tents."
    new "Los soldados heridos estaban alineados fuera de las tiendas de triaje."

    old "Already there were not enough medics to treat everyone."
    new "Ya no había suficientes médicos para atender a todos."

    old "Another loss like this and her army would be faced with some dire decisions."
    new "Otra pérdida de este tipo y su ejército se vería obligado a tomar algunas decisiones graves."

    old "Memories of the night before, replayed in her head."
    new "Los recuerdos de la noche anterior se repitieron en su mente."

    old "She had gotten the city, but at the expense of her dignity."
    new "Había conseguido la ciudad, pero a costa de su dignidad."

    old "Sarah prayed that everything that had transpired would remain a secret."
    new "Sarah oró para que todo lo ocurrido permaneciera en secreto."

    old "If her people ever found out..."
    new "Si su gente lo averiguara alguna vez..."
